Z||000000||vtail||01-10-2001||09:36 PM||||Started the car and turned on the headlights. Luckily just to move it in the driveway. When I shut it off the right side motor kept running in both open and closed position. The only way i can stop it is removing the fuse. Any ideas on the problem and the fix? 85 SE<BR>Thanks||||reg||1
Z||000001||fiero56||01-10-2001||09:38 PM||||You need rebuild kits from  <A HREF="http://www.rodneydickman.com" TARGET=_blank> Rodney Dickman</A><P><BR>What happened is that white plastic gear stripped out. It is possible to turn it around and use the good side, but I would replace those green bushings while you're in there, yours are probably bad by now anyway.<p>[This message has been edited by fiero56 (edited 01-10-2001).]||||reg||1
Z||000002||2xsess||01-11-2001||12:22 AM||||The same thing happened to me but I was 30 minutes away from home at a McDonalds. I tried the turning the gear 180 and it didn't do anything to help. Then I got Rodneys kit and I rebuilt the one that wasn't working Now it is so much smooother and quieter than the other one.<P>||||reg||1
